2026-09-23T07:48:36.3044925Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3045100Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3045319Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3045403Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3045510Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3045585Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3045684Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3045765Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3045871Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3045956Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046050Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046129Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046203Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046297Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046393Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046468Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046548Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046637Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046717Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046798Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3046961Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047056Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047133Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047228Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047308Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047452Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047624Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047706Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047801Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047892Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3047987Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3048082Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3048156Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3048265Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3048420Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3048501Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3048657Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3049571Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3049656Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3049730Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3049814Z     Features
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3049901Z     --------
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3049980Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3050572Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3050651Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3050745Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3051031Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3051135Z       of test modules and functions
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3051214Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3051482Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3051645Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3051723Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3051984Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3052080Z       test suites out of the box
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3052159Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3052254Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3052328Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3052810Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3052889Z     
2026-09-23T07:48:36.3052966Z     
